    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **21 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI introduced address normalization into the `POST /api/owners` OfficeFloor pipeline.\n\n**New shared helper** \u2014 `AddressNormalizer` (alongside the existing `TelephoneE164` / `OwnerEmail`):\n- Trims and collapses whitespace, upper-cases, and expands whole-word street abbreviations (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`). E.g. `\"  12  main  st \"` \u2192 `\"12 MAIN STREET\"`, `\"7 elm ave\"` \u2192 `\"7 ELM AVENUE\"`. A whitespace-only address normalizes to `\"\"` (treated as absent).\n\n**Wired into the three places that touch address:**\n1. `ValidateOwnerFields` \u2014 normalizes the address first, so the required-field check rejects an address that is **blank after normalization**, then stores the normalized form on the republished body (so `BuildOwner` maps it onto the entity, and it's persisted and returned).\n2. `EnsureUniqueHousehold` \u2014 duplicate detection now compares addresses via the normalized form.\n3. `AssignHousehold` \u2014 the shared `householdId` derivation and same-household matching now use the normalized form.\n\nBecause `ValidateOwnerFields` runs first, the stored address is already canonical; routing the comparisons through `AddressNormalizer` keeps them idempotent and correct against any historical data too. Javadoc on each class was updated to reflect the new behavior.\n\nTests covering this (`Cp01`, `Cp10`, `Cp11`, `Cp12`) and the rest of the suite all pass.",
